 "capsule": "The Northern Song (北宋, 960–1127) was founded by the general Zhao Kuangyin (Emperor Taizu), who seized power in a coup and reunified China after the chaos of the Five Dynasties, ruling from the capital Kaifeng. It presided over an era of economic growth, gunpowder and printing innovation, and a civil-service examination system that entrenched scholar-officials over the old aristocracy, though it never fully controlled the northern frontier lost to the Khitan Liao. The dynasty collapsed when the Jurchen Jin sacked Kaifeng in 1127, capturing Emperors Huizong and Qinzong in the Jingkang Incident and driving the Song court south.",
